From dfd49a3adb34ddcdb864c35ad02e523d20feee2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 19:14:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] netd: drop POSIX_SPAWN_CLOEXEC_DEFAULT to fix dnsmasq crash
 on some devices

On certain devices the dnsmasq child spawned by TetherController via
posix_spawn dies before exec() completes. Because the child never
writes to the error pipe, posix_spawn returns 0 to the parent yet the
child is already a zombie. This leaves mDaemonPid pointing to a dead
process and hotspot clients without DNS.

The surviving zombie retains the parent binder thread name
(e.g. "binder:1754_4") because exec() never ran, confirming the
failure path. No tombstones, avc denials, or logcat output from
dnsmasq appear.

Root cause
==========

POSIX_SPAWN_CLOEXEC_DEFAULT triggers bionic's posix_spawn child to
call close_range(3, ~0U, CLOSE_RANGE_CLOEXEC). On certain vendor
kernels the CLOSE_RANGE_CLOEXEC flag is not supported (it requires
Linux 5.11+ or a backported ACK), causing the child to _exit(127)
silently.

This flag was added by Google in Android 16. VoltageOS 5.9 (Android
15, branch 15) uses POSIX_SPAWN_USEVFORK without CLOEXEC_DEFAULT and
works correctly on the same device, confirming the diagnosis.

Fix
===

Remove POSIX_SPAWN_CLOEXEC_DEFAULT from the spawn flags. Keep
POSIX_SPAWN_USEVFORK for performance (matching the vfork path that
works on all tested devices).

Issue: #14
---
 server/TetherController.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/TetherController.cpp b/server/TetherController.cpp
index 2ee70af..5611b89 100644
--- a/server/TetherController.cpp
+++ b/server/TetherController.cpp
@@ -291,7 +291,7 @@ int TetherController::startTethering(bool usingLegacyDnsProxy, int num_addrs, ch
         return -res;
     }
     const android::base::ScopeGuard attrGuard = [&] { posix_spawnattr_destroy(&attr); };
-    res = posix_spawnattr_setflags(&attr, POSIX_SPAWN_USEVFORK | POSIX_SPAWN_CLOEXEC_DEFAULT);
+    res = posix_spawnattr_setflags(&attr, POSIX_SPAWN_USEVFORK);
     if (res) {
         ALOGE("posix_spawnattr_setflags failed (%s)", strerror(res));
         return -res;
-- 
2.54.0

